# Hex, Octal and Binary: whole numbers shown in base 16, 8 and 2. Each holds
# what an Integer holds; only how it is shown differs. `0xff`, `0o17` and
# `0b101` are literals of these types, in a cell and in a formula, with the
# prefix and the hex digits in either case and `_` among the digits.
#
# A negative one is shown as its 64-bit two's complement, as a format's `x`,
# `o` and `b` show it, and written in the file as `-0xff`, which reads back
# as the same number. Arithmetic on two of one base gives that base, and on
# any other mix an Integer. A format on the column replaces the prefix.

sheet Registers

Flags : Binary
Mode  : Octal
Wide  : Hex[08X]

| Name    | Addr    | Flags  | Mode  | Wide | Next | Mask | Plain | Count | Others | Double |
| ------- | ------- | ------ | ----- | ---- | ---- | ---- | ----- | ----- | ------ | ------ |
| control | 0x4000  | 0b0001 | 0o644 | 0xFF | *    | *    | *     | *     | *      | *      |
| status  | 0x4004  | 0b1010 | 0o755 | 255  | *    | *    | *     | *     | *      | *      |
| data    | 0x40_08 | 0b0100 | 0o600 | -0x1 | *    | *    | *     | *     | *      | *      |

Next   := Addr + 0x4
Mask   := Flags + 0b1
Plain  := Addr + 1
Count  := Addr.Integer
Others := Mode.Hex
Double := Wide * 0x2

sheet Totals

| All                   | Top                  | Neg    | Bin        |
| --------------------- | -------------------- | ------ | ---------- |
| =sum(Registers.Flags) | =max(Registers.Addr) | =-0xff | =Binary(5) |
